lesson: 251
title: Dozens and spoonfuls
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: A dozen is 12. Eggs, rolls, doughnuts and cookies are often sold by the dozen, so "3 dozen" means 3 × 12 = 36.
explain: To find how many are left, first turn the dozens into a number, then take away what was used or eaten.
explain: 2 dozen eggs, and 5 go into a cake: 2 × 12 = 24, and 24 − 5 = 19 eggs are left.
vars: a=name b=name d=2..6 u=2..30
need: u < d * 12 - 1
answer: d * 12 - u
exercise: {a} buys {d} dozen eggs and uses {u} of them for baking. How many eggs are left?
exercise: There are {d} dozen cookies on the plate. The children eat {u} of them. How many cookies are left on the plate?
exercise: {a}'s mother brings home {d} dozen bread rolls. {u} rolls are eaten at lunch. How many rolls remain?
exercise: A baker puts {d} dozen doughnuts in the window and sells {u} of them before noon. How many doughnuts are still in the window?
exercise: {a} and {b} bake {d} dozen muffins for the school fair. They give {u} muffins to the teachers. How many muffins do they have left?
exercise: Grandma had {d} dozen eggs in the fridge. She cracked {u} for pancakes. How many eggs are in the fridge now?
exercise: got {d} dozen eggs from the shop, used {u} for the cake n omelettes. how many left
exercise: mum got {d} dozen rolls for the bbq lol, we ate {u+1}, no wait {u}. how many rolls left
exercise: {d} dozen cookies in the tin, {a} n {b} scoffed {u} of em. how many still in there
exercise: so {a} brought {d} dozen donuts to footy, oh and it was raining heaps, anyway {u} got eaten. how many left over
exercise: nan bought {d} dozen eggs yeah, she used {u} for the trifle. hw many eggs she got left
exercise: we had {d} dozen muffins for the bake sale n sold {u}. how many we got left then
test: How many eggs remain after {u} are taken from {d} dozen?
test: {u} cookies have gone from a batch of {d} dozen. How many cookies are still there?
test: The class orders {d} dozen cupcakes for the party, and by home time {u} have been eaten. How many cupcakes are not eaten?
test: Of the {d} dozen eggs on the farm stall, {a} sells {u}. How many eggs does the stall still have?
test: {d} dozen eggs in the carton thingy, {u} broke on the way home ugh. how many ok ones
test: bakery gave us {d} dozen rolls, {u} gone already. how many we still got
test: {a} reckons {d} dozen is {d*10}. nah. we had {d} dozen bagels and ate {u}, how many left
exam: It is given that a quantity of {d.words} dozen eggs was procured, of which {u} were subsequently consumed in the preparation of a cake. Determine the number of eggs remaining.
exam: A consignment comprising {d} dozen bread rolls is delivered to a canteen. Whereas {u} rolls are dispensed at luncheon, ascertain the quantity of rolls retained.
exam: Compute the residual quantity of cookies, given an initial stock of {d} dozen and a subsequent depletion of {u} cookies.
exam: Pursuant to the purchase of {d} dozen muffins, {u} muffins were distributed to the teaching staff. State the number of muffins remaining in the possession of the purchasers.
exercise: {a} buys {d} dozen eggs, and {b} borrows {u} of them without asking and never brings them back. How many eggs does {a} still have?
exercise: {d} dozen cupcakes for the bake sale and that greedy pig {b} just tasted {u} of them. how many left, you muppet?
test: After Grandad's funeral (he passed away at ninety) the neighbours brought {d} dozen scones, and the mourners ate {u}. How many scones were left over?
